{
 "comment": "loans_interest #779 Phase A (vouchers both crediting and debiting a loan: listed, never netted), clause 31, a firm: two two-sided vouchers on one loan (cash in and bank out: possible s.269SS; bank in and cash out: possible s.269T), a row before the first (computed, with its balance figure), a cash repayment on its date and a bank repayment after both (each depends on them, naming only those on or before its date), a cash repayment exactly at the limit and a cash loan over it (computed on their own amount and flagged, no balance figure), no maximum outstanding (Mixed Loan); a two-sided voucher against an expense ledger and another loan's interest ledger whose other debits fall short of the credit (a forced set-off), then a cash loan walked from below zero, without the below-zero note (Below Zero Loan); a balanced voucher on the loan alone, not listed (Only Loan); an interest entry net of a TDS ledger outside Duties & Taxes with its reversal in the same voucher, keeping the interest reading, and an interest entry carrying another loan's line, listed, which leaves s.194A coverage not computed (Kappa Loan); a fully exempt lender's two-sided voucher, figures only (Bank Term Loan); a Government lender, 31(a) only and exempt from s.269SS/269T, with a forced set-off and a depending loan taken (Govt Loan); a voucher against only another loan's interest ledger on both sides (Misposted Loan).",
